      "body": "## What does this PR do?\n\n`/v1/completions` accepts several prompts in one request, but its usage record reported only the largest prompt's token count, and likewise for cached tokens. The `prompt_tokens` and `total_tokens` values therefore undercounted multi-prompt requests. This happened in both the streaming and non-streaming responses.\n\nThis PR sums prompt and cached tokens across the prompts of a completion request. Chat requests keep using the maximum, because their choices all share one prompt.\n\n## Example failure scenario(s)\n\n**Scenario (two-prompt completion)**\n\n- Client A sends a completion with two prompts of 3 and 2 tokens.\n- The engine generates 4 tokens in total.\n- Before this fix, usage reported `prompt_tokens: 3` and `total_tokens: 7`.\n- With this fix, usage reports `prompt_tokens: 5` and `total_tokens: 9`.\n\n## How was this bug discovered?\n\nThe completion response-format test sends prompts of different lengths and expects summed usage. The streaming fan-out test sends three requests and expects summed prompt and cached counts for completions, and the maximum for chat. On `main` both tests report only the largest prompt.\n\n## Dependency and scope\n\nThis PR is independent and based on `main`. It changes the usage totals in `completions.py` (non-streaming) and in `openai_streaming.py` (streaming, completions only). Two existing tests change only their expected completion prompt-token counts, because those expectations encoded the undercount: `test_completions_response_format` and `test_streaming_fans_out_and_reports_usage_on_request`. A new test, `test_streaming_usage_counts_cached_tokens_per_prompt`, checks the cached-token totals.\n\nThis PR and the following sibling PRs, also based on `main`, edit nearby lines. Whichever merges second needs a small merge-conflict resolution:\n- #8594: `test_endpoints_common.py`\n- #8596: `test_endpoints_common.py`\n- #8599: `openai_streaming.py`\n\n## Validation\n\nExact tested commit: `ad5dcb3d25ddeba06d6a7d140faa0cd4d103853e`.\n\n- **H100, job 20916673, and GB200, job 8372839:** `test_completions.py` and `test_endpoints_common.py` on 1 rank: 125 passed, 0 failed, 0 skipped on each.\n- **Fix-reverted control, H100 job 20916673:** with the production change reverted, all 6 completion cases failed at their usage checks:\n  - the two-prompt completion reported `prompt_tokens: 3` and `total_tokens: 7` instead of 5 and 9;\n  - the streamed three-prompt completion reported 2 prompt tokens instead of 6;\n  - its cached tokens were 3, the largest single prompt's count, instead of the sum 6.\n\n  The chat cases pass before and after the fix, because chat choices share one prompt.\n- Black, isort, Ruff and `git diff --check` pass.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
